  "title": "Bluetooth HCI Event: Add vendor-specific subevent dissector table to increase...",
  "description": "Bluetooth HCI Event: Add vendor-specific subevent dissector table to increase dissection flexibility\n\nPreviously, the vendor-spefic events are sent to be dissected based on the chip vendor.\nBut there are some types of events that needs to be considered by subevent code instead.\nOne prime example is Android's various hci events(https://source.android.com/docs/core/connect/bluetooth/hci_requirements#hci-event-vendor-specific),\nwhere the dissection should be tied to the subevent instead of the chip vendor.\n\nWith this change we try to dissect based on subevents first, then if there are no\ndissectors for the event we fall back to the previous logic of chip vendor.\nIt should make both public and private dissectors development easier.",
